#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:5
#: 0ff859e8fde941eca103b8a9f877fc25
msgid "Arming the motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:7
#: b59ab715ab624458a8c9749aca51c66d
msgid "Arming the vehicle allows the thrusters to start spinning.  Before arming, make sure all people, objects, and any body parts (e.g., hands) are clear of the thruster propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:9
#: adca6dae0cdc4075b5e55def32a5eaa2
msgid "In order to arm:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:11
#: a2089c43d6e14428969a7ede5796a3be
msgid "Pre-Arm safety checks must be passing (See :ref:`common-prearm-safety-checks`). It is recommended that :ref:`ARMING_SKIPCHK<ARMING_SKIPCHK>` be kept at 0 (no checks skipped) to prevent arming with system issues present. You must have also provided a method to Disarm the vehicle, either by GCS button assignments (``BTNx_FUNCTION``), or :ref:`AUX_FUNCTION <common-auxiliary-functions>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:12
#: 89efe961439c443a85569fed34f5fc43
msgid "The throttle must be at idle value if :ref:`RC_OPTIONS<RC_OPTIONS>` bit 5 is set (\"Arming check throttle for 0 input\"). Normally, this would be a center stick if bi-directional vertical thrusters are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:13
#: 150f2198ca4d41c39a82206a75104644
msgid "An arming pilot control must be activated, eg. GCS joystick button with \"Arm\" function assigned, GCS MAVLink ARM command given, or an :ref:`Auxiliary function <common-auxiliary-functions>` such as ARM/DISARM (\"153\") is used by either GCS command or RC channel switch (if enabled)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:16
#: 70e0021359de4154b519959ca46416bb
msgid "Disarming the motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:18
#: 79fad828834c457388cc55d14b7df4b1
msgid "Disarming the motors will prevent the motors from spinning. The motors are disarmed when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:20
#: 9c73f0b411f34b6b956dc7b1542f14a4
msgid "GCS joystick button with a \"Disarm\" function assigned is pressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:21
#: fa2cbc1a66ee4ce9ad2a1dcdf746ad94
msgid "A MAVLink DISARM command is received"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:22
#: 9f4146ee9d0847d69829b692e42e29c2
msgid "An :ref:`Auxiliary function <common-auxiliary-functions>` such as ARM/DISARM (\"153\") is used by either GCS command or RC channel switch (if enabled)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:25
#: 23719f3895674760a15c5fd174aece21
msgid "the AUX Function \"31\" (Motor Emergency Stop) or \"165\" (Arm/Motor Emergency Stop) can also be used to prevent motor operations, but do not \"Disarm\" which would reset the home location and require the pre-arming checks to be passed before re-arming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:28
#: d5a0e30b1ba04ef5b227f9b653c7e834
msgid "GCS Status Messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/arming-the-motors.rst:29
#: 3f9b6973092d40b195e2c50646f3a466
msgid "Unless the :ref:`ARMING_OPTIONS<ARMING_OPTIONS>` bit 2 is set, text messages will be sent to the GCS to indicate when arming or disarming has occurred."
msgstr ""
